    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d754">

                <pb facs="0808" n="704" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg704"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.94/499: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Latvia (Skinner) to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-04-20T16:00:00+02:00">April 20, 1932—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 20—2:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. Violent anti-Japanese campaign in <hi rendition="#italic">Izvestia</hi> April
                    15th and 18th, <hi rendition="#italic">Pravda</hi> 16th, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Trud</hi> 17th, claiming that Japanese military circles are more and more
                    in power, they want war, are inflaming public opinion, are responsible for
                    anti-Soviet activities of White Guards, are using Manchuria as base of
                    operations against Russia.</p>
                <p>Tass communiqué in <hi rendition="#italic">Izvestia</hi> April 18th that Soviets
                    have requested change of Chinese Consul in Blagoveshchensk on account of abuse
                    of code in sending messages purporting to be from General Ma.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
